RozeLynx netiface v13: attributed extension DNS lookups (browser.dns.resolve).

Extensions that resolve hostnames themselves (uBlock Origin's
dnsResolveEnabled — dnsResolve() calls browser.dns.resolve(hn,
['canonical_name']) from a blocking onBeforeRequest listener — AdGuard,
proxy checkers) pass no AdditionalInfo into Services.dns.asyncResolve, so
those lookups land in the unpartitioned (bindIface="") DNS partition and
egress the default route (global DoH or native UDP/53), leaking bound-tab
hostnames. All channel-driven lookups are already interface-bound (v11/v12).

Fix: consult the netiface component's host->binding activity index
(additionalInfoForHost) — recorded inside ResolveForChannel at channel
BeginConnect and AsyncOpen entry, most-recent-wins per host — and attach the
returned nsIDNSAdditionalInfo (per-interface resolver URL + bindIface) to
the lookup. Downstream machinery is unchanged: per-interface cache
partition, forced TRR-only for assigned records (NameLookup guard), bound
DoH channel (TRR::SendHTTPRequest), no native fallback.

When additionalInfoForHost returns null (host unattributed / never-bind /
feature or dnsAttribution off / build without USE=net-iface) the stock
unbound behavior is preserved. When attributed, RESOLVE_DISABLE_TRR is
stripped so a caller-requested native lookup cannot bypass the interface's
DoH path.

--- a/toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-dns.js
+++ b/toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-dns.js
@@ -32,6 +32,30 @@
             0
           );
 
+          // RozeLynx netiface v13: attribute extension DNS lookups
+          // (browser.dns.resolve — uBlock Origin's dnsResolveEnabled and
+          // anything else using the API) to the interface most recently
+          // used by a channel for this host. Without this the lookup
+          // carries no AdditionalInfo, lands in the unpartitioned DNS
+          // partition and egresses the default route — leaking bound-tab
+          // hostnames past per-interface DoH. Null (unattributed,
+          // never-bind, feature off, or build without net-iface) keeps
+          // stock behavior.
+          let additionalInfo = null;
+          try {
+            additionalInfo = Cc["@bytewheel.org/netiface;1"]
+              .getService(Ci.nsIRozeLynxNetIface)
+              .additionalInfoForHost(hostname);
+          } catch (e) {
+            // No netiface service (build without USE=net-iface) — unattributed.
+          }
+          if (additionalInfo) {
+            // Attributed lookups must ride the interface's DoH path; a
+            // caller-requested native lookup (disable_trr flag) would
+            // egress the default route.
+            dnsFlags &= ~Ci.nsIDNSService.RESOLVE_DISABLE_TRR;
+          }
+
           return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
             let request;
             let response = {
@@ -68,7 +92,7 @@
                 hostname,
                 Ci.nsIDNSService.RESOLVE_TYPE_DEFAULT,
                 dnsFlags,
-                null, // AdditionalInfo
+                additionalInfo, // RozeLynx netiface: attributed (or null)
                 listener,
                 null,
                 {} /* defaultOriginAttributes */
